Description: Disable the RTT-based frame-rate heuristic
 It lowers the encoder frame rate to 1-5 fps with Windows mstsc, which
 suspends frame acknowledgements, so every screen update lags about 1 s.
 Upstream removed the heuristic in 978f1cb7.
Origin: backport, https://invent.kde.org/plasma/krdp/-/commit/978f1cb7

--- a/src/VideoStream.cpp
+++ b/src/VideoStream.cpp
@@ -497,6 +497,10 @@
 
 void VideoStream::updateRequestedFrameRate()
 {
+    // Disabled, as upstream did in 978f1cb7: with Windows clients that suspend frame
+    // acknowledgements, RTT x frameDelay collapses the rate to 1-5 fps (about 1 s lag).
+    return;
+
     auto rtt = std::max(clk::duration_cast<clk::milliseconds>(d->session->networkDetection()->averageRTT()), clk::milliseconds(1));
     auto now = clk::system_clock::now();
 
